PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel remains in complete, unanimous agreement on Choice B (RGDSPSS). The systematic structure-activity relationship (SAR) design of the question tests the amino acid immediately following the invariant Arg-Gly-Asp motif at position 4 (Met, Ser, Leu, Gln, Ala). Among these, Ser-4 alongside Pro-5 forms the canonical fibronectin-derived RGDSP archetype, which enforces the critical type-II β-turn and specific hydrogen-bonding network necessary for high-affinity integrin engagement (particularly α5β1 and αvβ3). The alternative candidate, Choice C (RGDLTTP), is definitively ruled out: the authentic CAV-9 VP1 sequence terminates in TSTTRGDLTTS (ending in Ser/Ala, not Pro), and RGDL motifs require an extended amphipathic α-helix (RGDLxxL/I) that is destabilized by the C-terminal proline.
}

